    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region using the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), documenting the region-to-timezone mapping. This generates the `timezone` field on the `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired it into the MapStruct mapper:\n   - Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")`.\n   - Added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`).\n   - Added a `timezone(owner)` method that derives the IANA name from the owner's `locality(owner)` (which itself resolves region from postcode, falling back to the city table). Returns `null` for an unknown region so those owners serialize cleanly \u2014 consistent with the existing conventions for other derived nullable fields.\n\nThe new `Cp42Tests` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 `locality: NSW`, `timezone: Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite is green (56 tests, no failures).",
